Z||000015||FieroGT 914||07-23-2001||11:01 AM||||Hey - I just wanted to say thanks to Ski for allowing us to have that great picnic at his place.  I wish I would've known about the photo session at Zinn's later! (she would've looked great in front of my car too! hmmm... maybe she could come to Maple Grove with you this weekend - lol - with your's and her permission, of course  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<BR>I also have to say thanks to Jason for that great ride in the FEARO even though it started to get a little too hot when it was my turn for the ride - it's definitely the way I'll probably go for the engine conversion in my 87 GT.<BR>And to Jennifer, thanks, it was such a privilege to ride up with such a RARE Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hahaha.<BR>Kempo, you have to put that burnout video into a .avi or .mpeg format so we can all watch it on the computer!<BR>We have to get another one of these together again before I go back to school in August - I'd like to host it at my place too so drop a line and let me know if anyone would be interested in the PA BBQ II!<BR>Thanks, Joe<P>------------------<BR>Joe<P>AOL I.M.: FieroGT 914<BR>White 86 1/2 GT (Stock)<BR>Maroon 87 GT (Soon to be modified and hopefully receive a S/C 3800 or V8)||||reg||1
